      "message": "fix(2d): a stock-source pocket clears the stock around the setup's parts\n\nA 2D Pocket, 2D Adaptive or 2D Offset with the stock as its source\nbuilt the region from the whole stock footprint. The cut went through\nthe setup's parts, and generate said ok. Only the keep law (#1603)\nfound the gouge afterwards.\n\ncollect_job now builds the region of a stock-source pocket family op\nas the stock footprint minus the parts that stand in its step-down\nladder (area::stock_pocket, the same island law as the whole-model\npocket of #12). When no part stands in the ladder, the region is the\nstock footprint as before, so no golden changes. When the parts fill\nthe whole stock outline, generate refuses with a clear message.\n\nAn area offset into the part still gouges, and the keep law still\nrefuses the post. The second finding of the issue (a narrow outside\nband skipped with no note) moves to #1655.\n\nFixes #1554\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
